<body>
  <header><a class="brand" href="/"><span></span>StockTap</a><nav><a href="/problems/">Problems we fix</a><a href="/videos/">Videos</a><a href="/guides/">Guides</a><a href="/auth">Sign in</a></nav></header>
  <main>
    <div class="hero">
      <div>
        <span class="kicker">My stocktake says I&#x27;m down</span>
        <h1>Find out where the loss actually is.</h1>
        <p class="lead">A figure at the bottom of the report tells you you&#x27;re down. It doesn&#x27;t tell you which line, which day, or whether it&#x27;s a real loss or a button on the till. StockTap helps you find out.</p>
        <a class="btn" href="/auth?mode=signup" data-cta="problem-stocktake-down-top">Start free</a><a class="btn2" href="/#tour">Watch the tour</a>
        <p class="note">14 days of Pro free, no card. Cancel any time.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="phone"><video controls playsinline preload="metadata" poster="/media/poster-weighing-spot-check.jpg" src="/media/stocktap-weighing-spot-check.mp4" aria-label="Weighing and the next-day spot check"></video></div>
    </div>
    <h2>How StockTap sorts it</h2>
    <div class="steps">
      <div class="step"><b>Weigh, don&#x27;t guess</b><p>Put the open bottle on a kitchen scale and type the grams. StockTap gives you the millilitres left, the measures and the value, to the gram. Tenths by eye can&#x27;t see a few measures.</p></div>
      <div class="step"><b>Spot check the next day</b><p>Weigh the lines that move again, put in what the till rang, and StockTap shows the measures poured but not rung, in pounds.</p></div>
      <div class="step"><b>Catch it this week, not at month end</b><p>A few bottles a shift takes a couple of minutes, so drift gets caught while you can still do something about it.</p></div>
      <div class="step"><b>Never blames a person</b><p>StockTap shows lines, shifts and numbers. What you do with it is up to you.</p></div>
      <div class="step"><b>Use Venners? See where the result came from</b><p>Drop in their audit for up and down by category, the biggest losses and gains by line, and likely till-button mix-ups.</p></div>
    </div>
    <h2>What you need</h2>
    <div class="need">Your phone and any kitchen scale that reads grams. A Venners audit PDF if you have one.</div>
    <div class="cta">
      <h2 style="margin:0 0 6px">Try it on your own bar</h2>
      <p style="color:#8A9099">14 days of Pro free, no card. Cancel any time. Your phone is all you need to start.</p>
      <a class="btn" style="margin-top:14px" href="/auth?mode=signup" data-cta="problem-stocktake-down-bottom">Start free</a>
    </div>
    <h2>Other things StockTap sorts</h2>
    <div class="more">
      <a href="/problems/what-to-order">I never know what to order →</a>
      <a href="/problems/busy-weekends">Busy weekends catch me short →</a>
      <a href="/problems/checking-deliveries">Deliveries take ages to check →</a>
      <a href="/problems/postmix">Postmix never adds up →</a>
      <a href="/problems/venners-audit">Got a Venners audit? →</a>
    </div>
    <p class="author">Written by Shaun McManus, licensee in Washington, Tyne &amp; Wear, who built StockTap to run behind his own bar.</p>
  </main>
